    "title": "Count Equal XOR Prefix Pairs",
    "category": "Hashing",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer array, count the number of pairs of indices (i, j) such that the XOR of the prefix ending at i is equal to the XOR of the prefix ending at j, where i < j.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains integer N. \u2022 Second line contains N integers.",
    "output": "Print the total number of valid pairs.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 2\u00d710^5 \u2022 0 \u2264 nums[i] \u2264 10^9"
